1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, fame, power.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is a time known as
the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:35,260
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:40,460
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:55,257
Your heart will be your guide.

17
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:58,477
Raise the sails and take the helm.

18
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,137
That legendary place.

19
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,877
That the end of the map reveals.

20
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,737
Is only legendary.

21
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:10,117
Till someone proves it real.

22
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:13,877
Through it all, through all the trouble.

23
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:16,817
At times through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,117
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,280
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:28,217
So come aboard and bring along.

27
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,680
All your hopes and dreams.

28
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,877
Together we will find everything.

29
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,020
That we're looking for.

30
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,697
There's always room for you.

31
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,460
If you wanna be my friend.

32
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,800
We are, we are on a cruise.

33
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,720
We are.

34
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,440
This weather's perfect!

35
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:28,797
So which way is the
grand lot is it that way

36
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:34,697
or maybe this way that way over here maybe

37
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,737
there I don't know
where gonna be i want to

38
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:39,408
see this place i want
to see you need to sit

39
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:45,137
Jeez you bug me oh sorry
i'm just excited that we

40
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:48,360
finally got a cook on board
now we just need Nami!

41
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:51,816
Then nothing will stand
between us and the Grand Line!

42
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,380
Nami, I could just sit around all day
and think about how beautiful she is.

43
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:00,360
I can't wait till I get to see her again.

44
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:05,100
So, are we getting close to where Nami is?

45
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,515
You know, the island?

46
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:10,320
You're way too naive and way too young!

47
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,540
Don't you get it?

48
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:16,504
Don't you realize every second that passes
brings us closer to the infamous R-log?

49
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:23,097
Nami couldn't stop looking at
Arlong's picture when she saw it.

50
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:25,356
And it wasn't a normal kind of stare.

51
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:28,837
There was something different
about the way she was staring.

52
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:29,979
Something focused.

53
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:34,960
I'm telling you,

54
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,097
Nami's planning on taking down Arlong and

55
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,337
then collecting the 20
million berry bounty.

56
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:41,517
For all we know, while we just sit here,

57
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:44,541
she's already making her
way through his compound.

58
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:46,530
That's nice.

59
00:03:46,613 --> 00:03:47,443
Let's eat.

60
00:03:47,526 --> 00:03:48,356
Sounds good.

61
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:49,850
Ah!

62
00:03:49,933 --> 00:03:51,617
Don't tell me you guys
are so clueless that you

63
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:53,937
have actually never
heard of the evil Arlong!

64
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:55,300
Uh, no. Nope.

65
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,500
Listen up, boys!

66
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:06,489
Time for your education on the
cunning shark that is Arlong.

67
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:08,897
Arlong is a fishman who used to destroy

68
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:11,477
everything in his path up
and down the Grand Line.

69
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,900
Fishman? That's cool.

70
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,837
I don't think I've ever
met one of those before.

71
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:18,097
I've heard that the females
on Fishman Island are some

72
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:20,757
of the most beautiful creatures
in the world to behold.

73
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,360
Fishman sounds weird.

74
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:24,400
Do they look like this?

75
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:28,117
Can't you focus for just one minute,

76
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:32,677
please all right I will start
from the very beginning the reason

77
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:35,657
they call the Grand Line of pirate
graveyard in the first place

78
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:38,857
Is because of our long and the
other two powers like him who rule

79
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:42,660
over it the first of the powers
are known as the seven warlords

80
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,020
Seven Warlords?

81
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:52,640
The Seven Warlords are pirates
authorized by the government. Seriously?

82
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:56,453
Why would any pirate on the
sea want government approval?

83
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:58,340
For protection.

84
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:02,157
The government looks the other way in
exchange for a cut of their treasure,

85
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,946
and they're allowed to exist.

86
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:06,817
Of course, to other pirates,
they're just government dogs.

87
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:09,837
But they didn't get to where
they are by being weak.

88
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:11,332
These guys are powerful.

89
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:20,480
The man who defeated Zoro
is one of these warlords.

90
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:22,660
His name is Hawkeye Mihawk.

91
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:23,920
That's so cool!

92
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:26,897
I can't wait to meet
all seven of these guys!

93
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:28,140
They sound awesome!

94
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:32,657
Yeah, well, the first among the warlords,
at least first you should know about?

95
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:34,740
is Jinbei, captain of the Fishmen.

96
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:37,780
He is dangerous like no
one you've ever known?

97
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:40,397
Easily causing as much
havoc and destruction!

98
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,420
around the Grand Line as Arlong.

99
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,802
Is this closer?

100
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,057
That looks just like your last
picture, only standing up.

101
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:53,375
Arlong has taken control of over 20
towns since coming to the East Blue.

102
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:56,117
His strength easily surpasses
anyone you've encountered,

103
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,717
including that of Don Crocus.

104
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,800
He's devastating.

105
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:03,219
So why do you think Nami would go
after this guy all by herself, huh?

106
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,157
I told you already.

107
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,497
She wants to collect
the bounty on his head.

108
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:10,257
Oh, wouldn't it be great
if Nami was a mermaid?

109
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:12,320
I'd give anything to see that.

110
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:15,937
She'd look like this.

111
00:06:16,020 --> 00:06:18,340
Tear that thing up or die!

112
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:21,937
Have either of you morons heard a
single word that I've said to you?

113
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:23,440
Sure, badass fish man.

114
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:24,937
Some guy's stronger than some other guy.

115
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:25,850
We get it.

116
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,620
No, you don't get it.

117
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:30,018
You've never had to face a fish man.

118
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:34,200
Well, we will when we get
there, so don't worry about it.

119
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:37,060
I guess I'll get lunch started.

120
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:40,600
About time. Let's eat. What? Food?

121
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:42,437
What are you in the mood for?

122
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:44,800
I want meat right off the bone!

123
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,569
I want salty bean sprouts!

124
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,275
Okay, leave it to me.

125
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:51,680
This won't take long.

126
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,577
Meat and bean sprouts, no problem.

127
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:56,900
Man, having a cook is the best! Huh? Huh?

128
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:58,520
It sure is!

129
00:06:58,760 --> 00:06:59,660
Bring me meat!

130
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:01,720
Lots of meat! Sprouts!

131
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:03,060
I want bean sprouts!

132
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,911
Here's this month's take.

133
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,600
I hope you enjoy it.

134
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:26,249
Ah, Arlong, you are so much smarter than
your regular run-of-the-mill pirate.

135
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:28,900
You know how the world works.

136
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:33,090
Likewise,

137
00:07:33,173 --> 00:07:35,297
there aren't many marine captains
who know that befriending

138
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:38,321
me means they can milk the
East Blue for eternity.

139
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:42,977
The fact that you understand makes you more
like me than any other marine out here.

140
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:44,380
Thank you very much.

141
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,340
Don't thank me. Thank money.

142
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:51,017
It's the only thing you
can count on in this world.

143
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,960
It's more reliable than
people, that's for sure.

144
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,240
Don't you agree?

145
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,160
Of course.

146
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,857
As a rule, I hate all humans.

147
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:04,037
But you are the one tolerable
exception that I found.

148
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:07,057
Well, if you'll excuse me.

149
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:10,080
Why not stay a while and
have a drink with me?

150
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:14,197
I would, but the longer a marine
cruiser stays docked at a pirate island,

151
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,297
the quicker we get unwanted attention.

152
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:18,197
I'll kill anyone who reports you.

153
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:19,515
Everybody knows that.

154
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:22,640
Thank you, but still, we must go. Hey!

155
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:24,373
The captain is leaving.

156
00:08:24,620 --> 00:08:26,267
Escort him back to his ship.

157
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:27,700
Yes, sir!

158
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:32,700
The pot's back that
way. Hop in. Thank you.

159
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:34,217
That's very kind of you.

160
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:37,397
When I see your face, it
always makes me want to laugh.

161
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,310
It's funny.

162
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:39,476
You look like a rat.

163
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:43,880
Hey, Hachi, watch your mouth now.

164
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:45,957
The captain's our honored guest.

165
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,140
Oh, right.

166
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:48,460
Sorry about that.

167
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:49,855
Don't worry about it.

168
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,660
Here we go, man.

169
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:58,360
These fishmen are disgusting.

170
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:02,140
Such a vile group, but
they sure do pay well.

171
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:18,710
Hey, you!

172
00:09:18,793 --> 00:09:19,699
Get out of my way!

173
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,167
Arlong's going to die today!

174
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:26,668
He killed my daddy, and so now
I'm going to have to kill him!

175
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:31,020
So move, or I'll have to kill you too!

176
00:09:31,980 --> 00:09:32,810
Hey!

177
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,230
Now,

178
00:09:37,313 --> 00:09:39,057
you should know that
Arlong doesn't have time

179
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:41,846
to deal with whimpering
little punks like you.

180
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:44,520
You're too young. Go home.

181
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:50,441
Take that with you and use it to
keep yourself out of trouble, kid.

182
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:52,080
Go to hell!

183
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,300
Nami, you've returned.

184
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:04,217
I haven't seen you around
here for quite a while.

185
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:06,240
So, how did you do this time?

186
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:08,060
Who are you talking to?

187
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:12,693
You know, I can't believe the world
is full of such blind idiots, modesty.

188
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:17,840
You girl are one excellent
liar. That's true.

189
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,200
Listen up, everybody!

190
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,020
Nami's finally returned!

191
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,200
Time for a party!

192
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,220
All right, we're here.

193
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:52,300
That's Arlong Park ahead.

194
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:56,160
Arlong Park, huh?

195
00:10:56,360 --> 00:11:00,595
So this is the hideout of Arlong the
Fishman Pirate from the Grand Line?

196
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:03,240
I hope Nomi's really here.

197
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:09,260
Big Sis-Nami's ship was the Going
Mary, so before we do anything stupid,

198
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:12,597
we should quietly check to see if
it stopped on this island first.

199
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:13,621
Yeah, good idea.

200
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:20,080
Let's attack.

201
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,740
But I just said we shouldn't
do anything stupid!

202
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:26,150
What?

203
00:11:26,233 --> 00:11:27,140
Attack, you idiot!

204
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:29,177
We know nothing about this place!

205
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:31,400
Yeah, these guys are the fishmen!

206
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:33,197
We need some kind of plan to do that!

207
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:36,377
While the two of you are busy
blabbering and wimping out,

208
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:39,357
I'm placing my thoughts on the
battle we're about to face.

209
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:42,616
Luffy told me to bring her
back and I'll do just that.

210
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:44,750
Let's go!

211
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:53,160
There it is!

212
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:55,760
Ha! Found it! The Going Mary!

213
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:56,877
It's right over there!

214
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:58,897
Then she has to be on
the island somewhere.

215
00:11:58,980 --> 00:12:00,437
We just have to find her.

216
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,797
What do you think you're doing?

217
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:03,017
Would you idiots untie me?

218
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,260
I am not the enemy!

219
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:08,340
We're east of Arlong Park
here at Cocoyashi Village.

220
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:09,840
But it's strange.

221
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:13,240
Why would she have stopped
so far from the village?

222
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:15,600
Untie me, dammit!

223
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:19,537
Zoro, you're hurt way too bad to
be of any help when we go ashore.

224
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:21,240
Just sit tight and relax.

225
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:24,030
It's okay.

226
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,420
Rista, you can help next time.

227
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:31,837
One of these days, I'm going to
skewer him like a piece of meat.

228
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:33,017
Fear not, gentlemen.

229
00:12:33,100 --> 00:12:35,159
I will bring back the girls safely.

230
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:40,060
Looks like skipping Arlong
Park has sure cheered you up.

231
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:41,660
Prepare the anchor.

232
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,160
Bring us alongside the Going Merry.

233
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:45,890
Aye.

234
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:48,400
Ah, yes.

235
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:52,157
Now that we're underway, it's time
to give a name to this voyage.

236
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:55,887
I think I shall call it the Great
Adventures of Captain Usopp.

237
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:05,530
What is it?

238
00:13:05,613 --> 00:13:06,443
What'd you see?

239
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:08,800
It's fishmen!

240
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:11,600
Full speed ahead!

241
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:12,740
Okie Dock.

242
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,278
Why didn't we just dock right there?

243
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:19,940
Didn't you see that?

244
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:21,677
There were three fishmen over there!

245
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:22,878
It's Arlong's crew!

246
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,786
We can't stop here right now!

247
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,720
Do not yell at me!

248
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:31,257
If there are fishmen here, this entire
area must be under Arlong's control,

249
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:32,220
so what now?

250
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:35,980
We could just say we couldn't find her.

251
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:38,540
Untie me now, morons! Come on!

252
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:43,380
Never seen that boat before. Suspicious.

253
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:46,740
Let's run!

254
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:50,060
Okay, untie me! Damn it!

255
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:53,670
Fight!

256
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:55,350
Hey!

257
00:13:55,433 --> 00:13:57,651
You two get back here or you're gonna die!

258
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:05,000
There's just this one guy.

259
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:08,457
